#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-store-repair.md:28
msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-store-repair.md:30
msgid ""
"This command attempts to \"repair\" the store paths specified by "
"[_installables_](./nix.md#installables) by redownloading them using the "
"available substituters. If no substitutes are available, then repair is not "
"possible."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-store-repair.md:35
msgid "**Warning**"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-store-repair.md:37
msgid ""
"During repair, there is a very small time window during which the old path "
"(if it exists) is moved out of the way and replaced with the new path. If "
"repair is interrupted in between, then the system may be left in a broken "
"state (e.g., if the path contains a critical system component like the GNU C "
"Library)."
msgstr ""

